# V90Demodulator: the V.90 / V.92 receive side (phase 3 line probing -> phase 4 -> data), 0x298 bytes on i386, a plain class (no vptr, no base class); V90Modem embeds it.  It EMBEDS six objects
# (flattened here, `align8` = the sub-object holds pointers: 8-aligned and padded on x86-64): an Agc<float> (+0x4c, P03), a V90PreFilter (+0x6c, P22; a FloatFIR is its base), a V90Resampler (+0x94, P05; vptr),
# a V90ConstellationPower (+0x148, P06), a Descrambler<unsigned char, int> (+0x1e8, P01) and a V90SpectralVerifier (+0x210, P21).  The heap objects it owns are pointers: V90Equalizer (+0x1d8, P40),
# V90Phase3Demodulator (+0x1dc, P34), V90Phase4Demodulator (+0x1e0, P37), V90Demapper (+0x1e4, P28), V90ConstellationDesigner (+0x208, P24), V90ConnectionEvaluator (+0x20c, P17),
# V90AutoDigitalImpDetector (+0x23c, P18), V90TRN2Designer (+0x1c, P26) and six sample buffers (+0x244 .. +0x25c).  Names are by use (see porting/decompiled/dp/p43_demodulator_progress.txt).
